# DIAGNOSTICS

At start it prints the disk, how the volume is read, its label if it has one, and its size in sectors.
A failure to start prints `isofs: FAILED:` and what failed, with the error when there is one, and exits with what failed:

: `no connector to a disk (connect=)`
  The manifest connects it to no disk.
: `no listen channel (post=)`
  The manifest posts nothing.
: `cannot open a session on the disk`
  The block session was refused.
: `the disk's sectors do not divide 2048`
  The disk's sectors are larger than ISO 9660's, or not a divisor of them.
: `no ISO 9660 volume on the disk`
  There is no volume descriptor at sector 16, or no primary one; followed by `operation not supported`, the volume's logical blocks are not 2048 bytes.

An argument it does not know prints the usage message, after `isofs: FAILED:`, and exits with it.
It exits `cannot serve` if serving fails.

# BUGS

A file of more than one extent, past 4 GiB, is read only to its first extent.

There is no zisofs, no UDF, no ISO level 3, and El Torito's boot images are not served as files.

Rock Ridge is checked only against the specification, 9660srv's reading and Limine; no reader of it on the build host checks the writer `./build` uses for its ISOs, so a misreading the two share would go unseen.

A CD drive needs virtio-scsi, which has no driver, so ISOs are read from disks.
